        "evidence": "AST analysis confirms parallel wavefront refinement for `inner_recurrence` steps followed by sampling `headway` positions, but the logbook itself flags that 'decoding occurs after the inner-recurrence loop, not after every single inner step,' creating ambiguity with the claim's 'every forward pass' wording, and no execution was performed.",
        "status": "inconclusive",
        "target_claim": "The sampler decodes new tokens every forward pass while refining latent states for those tokens in parallel through recurrent depth (Section 3.1)."
      },
      {
        "claim": "The paper proves the sampler is strictly more expressive than baseline autoregressive generation under the same time budget on modern hardware (Theorem 4.2).",
        "evidence": "The logbook explicitly states 'No independent proof or hardware timing reproduction was completed' and notes a theorem-numbering discrepancy (Theorem 4.2 vs 4.4), so the expressiveness proof was never reproduced or independently verified.",
        "status": "inconclusive",
        "target_claim": "The paper proves the sampler is strictly more expressive than baseline autoregressive generation under the same time budget on modern hardware (Theorem 4.2)."
      }
